---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import { site, links } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`Why ${site.company} exists, and who is behind it.`}>
  <Hero
    label="About"
    title="Most of the job is detective work."
    subtitle="Something in the funnel does not add up. The work is finding out why, proving it, and fixing it so it stays fixed."
  />

  <Section label="The story" narrow>
    <div class="prose">
      <!-- Placeholder copy: owner to replace with their own story. -->
      <p>
        {site.company} started from a pattern that kept repeating. A marketing team would ask why a
        campaign looked like it underperformed, or why lead counts in the CRM did not match the form
        tool. The answer was almost never the campaign. It was a tag firing twice, a hidden field that
        stopped populating after a site update, or a form that showed a thank-you message while the CRM
        received nothing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Finding those problems means following the evidence: reading network requests, comparing
        timestamps across systems, submitting test leads and tracing where they go. It is closer to an
        investigation than to a report.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is the work {site.company} does, for clients directly through audits and fixes, and at scale
        through {site.product}, which captures the evidence most tools throw away.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section tone="tint" label="Point of view" title="Funnel clarity comes before optimization.">
    <div class="pov">
      <div>
        <h3>Measure what happened</h3>
        <p>Before deciding what to change, know what actually occurred. Most teams are optimizing against data with gaps in it.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Count the people who left</h3>
        <p>Converters are only part of the story. The visitors who dropped off are where the leaks are.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Be honest about the data</h3>
        <p>Attribution is a model, not a fact. Good reporting says what it knows, what it assumes, and where it is unsure.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section narrow>
    <div class="end">
      <p>If your funnel has a number nobody trusts, that is a good place to start.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <Button href={links.bookAudit}>Book an audit</Button>
        <Button href="/labs" variant="secondary">Read {site.labs}</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style lang="scss">
  .prose p {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: $gray-700;
  }

  .pov {
    display: grid;
    gap: $space-6;

    @include md {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }

    > div {
      border-top: 2px solid $navy;
      padding-top: $space-4;
    }

    p {
      color: $gray-700;
      margin: 0;
    }
  }

  .end p {
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: $space-3;
  }
</style>
